# Every env file, not just `.env`.
#
# A backup called `.env.backup` or `.env.old` is the same secrets under a name
# the old single line did not match — which is how a merchant secret ends up in
# a public repository. The example file is the one exception: it holds names,
# never values.
.env*
!.env.example
key-base64.txt
